{%- comment -%}
  The Click-Key Blocks card, rendered twice on the home page: once in the
  #new band under the hero, once again just above the endless bubble
  band. One source rather than two copies that drift apart the first time
  the copy or the price changes.

  The product is re-assigned here rather than passed in because a snippet
  cannot see variables assigned by the section -- p_ckb does not cross
  the render boundary. Global objects do, which is what all_products is,
  and so does the section object the settings below come from. This is
  the same arrangement snippets/wt-bubble.liquid uses.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% assign ckb = all_products['click-key-blocks'] %}
<article class="wt-new__card">
  <div class="wt-new__media">{% if ckb.featured_image %}<img src="{{ ckb.featured_image | image_url: width: 800 }}" width="{{ ckb.featured_image.width }}" height="{{ ckb.featured_image.height }}" alt="{{ ckb.title }}" class="wt-new__img">{% else %}{% render 'wt-img', img: section.settings.new_image, label: 'Click-Key Blocks photo &mdash; SKU 740', fit: 'contain' %}{% endif %}</div>
  <div class="wt-new__body">
    <p class="wt-new__eyebrow">Just landed &middot; available now</p>
    <h2 class="wt-new__title">click-key blocks</h2>
    <p class="wt-new__copy">{{ section.settings.new_copy }}</p>
  </div>
  <div class="wt-new__buy">
    <span class="wt-new__price">{{ ckb.price | money_without_trailing_zeros }}</span>
    <a href="{{ ckb.url }}" class="wt-btn wt-btn--nowrap">Shop Click-Key Blocks</a>
  </div>
</article>
